ation and delivery to Slack; Vector adds contact-level intent and ad-audience activation, which is most of what the price gap buys."}],"blogName":"RB2B vs Vector: which should you choose in 2026?"}},"heroImage":{"url":"https://images.ctfassets.net/kyprwggh4muz/48ekBZNJ31NthxfZJw6TpY/80aaa503aa82ec87950563f3f4651840/rb2b-vs-vector-cover.webp","width":2389,"height":1120,"title":"RB2B vs Vector: which should you choose in 2026?"},"content":{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"RB2B and Vector both identify individual, named visitors on US website traffic, but they sit at different price points and depths. RB2B is a low-cost, Slack-first identification tool that starts free. Vector layers person and contact-level intent data on top and costs far more. Choose by budget and whether you need intent signals.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"How do RB2B and Vector compare at a glance?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Tool","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Best for","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Identification level","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Standout capability","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Published pricing","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"RB2B","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Lean teams wanting cheap, fast, named US visitor ID pushed to Slack","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Person-level, US traffic","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Free entry tier; instant Slack delivery of named visitors","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Free; Starter $79/mo; Pro $149/mo; Pro+ $199/mo (per rb2b.com)","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Vector","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Teams that want named visitors plus intent data and ad activation","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Person and contact-level, US traffic","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Person-level ID combined with intent signals and ad-audience activation","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Platform fee plus usage credits; mid-sized deployments near $6,000/mo (per vector.co)","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"}],"nodeType":"table"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"What is the core difference between RB2B and Vector?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Both resolve anonymous US website traffic to named individuals, which is a step beyond the company-level tools common in Europe. Where they diverge is depth and price.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{"target":{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"kyprwggh4muz"}},"id":"67AAsohpr3T2s1f7PlMaNs","type":"Asset","createdAt":"2026-09-20T01:39:08.935Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-20T01:39:08.935Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":2,"revision":1,"locale":"en-US"},"fields":{"title":"RB2B vs Vector key points","description":"Infographic for the RB2B vs Vector comparison","file":{"url":"//images.ctfassets.net/kyprwggh4muz/67AAsohpr3T2s1f7PlMaNs/c1e4b35904ff863fb92459f31caff5b4/rb2b-vs-vector-infographic.png","details":{"size":99295,"image":{"width":1080,"height":1080}},"fileName":"rb2b-vs-vector-infographic.png","contentType":"image/png"}}}},"content":[],"nodeType":"embedded-asset-block"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"RB2B is deliberately narrow. It identifies the person, attaches a business email and social profile, and pushes that to Slack or Teams in near real time. The pioneer of the person-level category, it built its following on speed, simplicity, and a free tier. It stops at identification; what you do with the name is up to you.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Vector is heavier. It does person and contact-level identification too, but wraps it in intent data, so you see not just who visited but what they appear to be researching, and it can push identified and intent-scored audiences into advertising and CRM workflows. Its identified and intent-scored audiences are built to feed paid channels such as LinkedIn and Google Ads, not just a Slack alert. You pay considerably more for that added intelligence and activation.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"How do RB2B and Vector price in 2026?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The gap is large. RB2B's free plan gives you 150 monthly resolutions at the company level, pushed to Slack, at no cost. Paid tiers add person-level identification: Starter at $79/month (300 resolutions), Pro at $149/month (600-plus resolutions with business emails and all integrations), and Pro+ at $199/month for premium resolution and higher volumes, per its pricing page. Paid plans include a 7-day trial.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Vector starts where RB2B tops out, and it no longer sells fixed tiers. Pricing is a flat platform fee plus usage credits, sized on an interactive calculator against your tracked accounts, monthly site visits, signal volume, and number of bid agents. Vector's own sample scenario, 8,000 tracked accounts and 51,000 monthly visits with moderate signals and five bid agents, lands around $6,300 per month. Credits roll over month to month on monthly plans, with a 30-day expiry; annual plans release the full year's credits upfront. Higher volumes move to sales-assisted annual pricing. The practical read: Vector is sized to your traffic rather than to a plan name, which suits teams with a clear volume estimate and frustrates those wanting a number off a page.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Put simply: RB2B is a low-commitment tool you can start free; Vector is a mid-market intent platform priced accordingly.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Which has better data and match rates?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Be skeptical of both vendors' coverage claims. RB2B publishes person-level coverage in the range of 15-45% depending on plan tier, a vendor figure, while independent tests of the category land closer to 5-20% of US traffic for person-level identification. Vector's numbers should be read the same way. Both are strong for US B2B traffic and weak to nonexistent for international visitors, because the identity graphs behind person-level resolution are US-centric.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Where Vector pulls ahead is not raw match rate but enrichment. It adds contact-level intent signals, so an identified visitor comes with a read on what they are researching, which RB2B does not provide. If your motive is simply \"tell me who is on my site, cheaply, in Slack,\" RB2B's data is enough. If you want to prioritize by buying intent and feed ad audiences, Vector's added layer is the point.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"How do RB2B and Vector handle privacy and CIPA?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Person-level identification carries more legal exposure than the company-level approach, and both tools live in that harder zone. Naming individual US visitors has drawn scrutiny under a wave of CIPA pixel litigation in California, per legal-industry coverage, and GDPR effectively rules out person-level identification for European traffic, which is why both tools restrict named resolution to US IP addresses.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"RB2B has been public about the constraint: its contact-level identification is US-only, with company-level identification available globally. Vector's person-level match is likewise US-centric. Neither offers meaningful named identification of EU visitors, and you should not expect them to. If your traffic is largely non-US, or your counsel is wary of person-level tracking, this whole category is a poor fit and company-level tools are the safer route.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Which should you choose, RB2B or Vector?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Choose RB2B if you want the cheapest, fastest way to see named US visitors in Slack, you are testing whether person-level identification is even useful for you, or you want to start free before committing budget. It is the pragmatic pick for small teams and early experiments.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Choose Vector if you have budget for a mid-market tool, you want intent data layered onto identification, and you plan to activate identified audiences in advertising and CRM, not just react to alerts. Its monthly plans, with credits that roll over, make that easier to trial than an annual contract.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Both stop short of doing the outreach. Whichever you pick, the identified name lands in your tools and your team works it from there. If the goal is meetings rather than a list of names, that is a different job.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"An autonomous platform is the third path: Artisan is an AI outbound platform that identifies visitors, person-level on US traffic and company-level globally on a 3.7-billion-IP identity graph, qualifies them against your ICP, and has its ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/ai-sales-agent"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"AI sales agent","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" (Ava, an AI BDR) run the email follow-up and inbound chat. It buys activation, not just identification and intent, which makes it a heavier commitment than either tool here but removes the manual step both leave you. Artisan runs on usage-based credits, with no per-seat platform fee and a free trial to start. For the wider category, see our roundup of ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/blog/the-best-website-visitor-identification-tools"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"the best website visitor identification tools","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":".","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Frequently asked questions","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Is RB2B or Vector better for person-level identification?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Both do US person-level identification. RB2B is cheaper and simpler, pushing named visitors to Slack. Vector costs more but adds contact-level intent data and ad activation. For raw \"who visited,\" RB2B is enough; for prioritizing by intent and feeding paid channels, Vector's extra layer is what you are paying for.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Does RB2B have a free plan?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Yes. RB2B offers a free tier at $0/month with 150 monthly resolutions at the company level, delivered to Slack, per its pricing page. Person-level identification with business emails starts on the paid Starter ($79/month) and Pro ($149/month) plans. Vector has no free plan and no fixed entry tier; it charges a platform fee plus usage credits sized to your traffic.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Do RB2B and Vector work outside the US?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Person-level identification is effectively US-only for both, because the underlying identity graphs are US-centric and GDPR limits person-level tracking in Europe. RB2B offers company-level identification globally. If most of your traffic is international, neither tool's headline feature will match well.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"What person-level match rate is realistic?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Independent testing suggests roughly 5-20% of US traffic for person-level identification, below the higher figures vendors publish (RB2B, for example, cites 15-45% by tier). International person-level match is near zero. Use trials to measure on your own traffic before committing.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Is Vector worth the price premium over RB2B?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"It depends on whether you will use the extra capability. Vector's cost buys contact-level intent data and ad-audience activation on top of identification. If you only need named visitors in Slack, RB2B does that for a fraction of the price. If intent scoring and paid-channel activation drive your motion, Vector earns the premium.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Is there an alternative to both RB2B and Vector?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Yes. Both identify visitors and route them to your tools; the outreach is on you either way. Artisan takes the other approach: it identifies visitors, person-level on US traffic and company-level globally, qualifies them against your ICP, then has its ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/blog/ai-bdr"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"AI BDR","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" run the follow-up and inbound chat. It is a bigger commitment than a Slack-alert tool or an intent platform, so it fits teams that want the booked meeting rather than the name.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The bottom line","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"RB2B is the low-cost, Slack-first way to see named US visitors, and it starts free. Vector is the pricier, intent-rich option for teams that want to prioritize and activate those visitors in advertising and CRM. Both are US-centric for person-level identification, and both carry the privacy considerations that come with naming individuals. If you want identification to become booked meetings without more headcount, look at an autonomous ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/blog/ai-bdr"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"AI BDR","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" that owns the follow-up, and compare models on the ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/pricing"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"pricing page","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":".","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"document"},"authors":[{"id":"2BNzbXmPpTiXXI35GfMMwO","slug":"jaspar-carmichael-jack","authorName":"Jaspar Carmichael-Jack","authorDesignation":"Co-Founder & CEO @ Artisan","authorDescription":"Jaspar is an entrepreneur with expertise in sales, marketing, and operations. He founded Artisan in 2023, a company automating workflows with AI employees.","profileImageUrl":"https://ca.slack-edge.com/T05QXKPJQNN-U05RMB3DP1N-83c0c4161322-512","authorSocials":{"twitter":"https://x.com/jasparcjack","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jaspar-carmichael-jack"}}],"fields":{"blogNavigation":{"fields":{"contentNavigation":[{"label":"How do RB2B and Vector compare at a glance?","link":"#how_do_rb2b_and_vector_compare_at_a_glance?"},{"label":"What is the core difference between RB2B and Vector?","link":"#what_is_the_core_difference_between_rb2b_and_vector?"},{"label":"How do RB2B and Vector price in 2026?","link":"#how_do_rb2b_and_vector_price_in_2026?"},{"label":"Which has better data and match rates?","link":"#which_has_better_data_and_match_rates?"},{"label":"How do RB2B and Vector handle privacy and CIPA?","link":"#how_do_rb2b_and_vector_handle_privacy_and_cipa?"},{"label":"Which should you choose, RB2B or Vector?","link":"#which_should_you_choose_rb2b_or_vector?"},{"label":"Frequently asked questions","link":"#frequently_asked_questions"},{"label":"The bottom line","link":"#the_bottom_line"}]}}}},{"id":"4Wrn91fQ5zB1qzJaHEnxHX","slug":"artisan-vs-unify","title":"Artisan vs Unify: which fits your team?","metaTitle":"Artisan vs Unify: which fits your team in 2026?","publishedDate":"2026-09-20","seoDescription":"A stage-by-stage comparison of Artisan and Unify. Where Unify's signal-based plays win, where Artisan's AI-run outreach wins, and how to choose.","readTime":"6 minutes","tag":"Comparisons","keyTakeAways":{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"kyprwggh4muz"}},"id":"eQ6A3UnR6Go1IQjJE0rdK","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-09-20T02:01:41.137Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-20T02:01:41.137Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":1,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"blogKeyTakeaways"}},"locale":"en-US"},"fields":{"keyTakeAways":[{"keyTakeAways":"Unify is a warm-outbound system of action: it aggregates intent and buying signals, then runs automated plays across email and social outreach. It's a solid signal-driven engine, backed by a $40M Series B (Battery, July 2025), with customers including Cursor, Perplexity, Flock Safety, Airwallex, and Together AI."},{"keyTakeAways":"Unify is still ops-configured. It's a powerful tool your team sets up and maintains, not an AI employee that owns the job."},{"keyTakeAways":"Artisan detects signals and runs the outreach end to end. Ava enriches, personalizes, sends across channels, handles replies, dials the call steps for a rep to take over, and books meetings."},{"keyTakeAways":"Unify's public pricing now starts at Free for up to 3 seats, Base at $20/seat/month, and Pro at $60/seat/month, with Business custom, plus credits. (The old ~$700/month figure is obsolete.)"},{"keyTakeAways":"Artisan is usage-based: you pay for work performed, not seats, and there is no per-seat platform fee."},{"keyTakeAways":"Artisan supports natural-language custom signals: define any trigger in plain English, with confidence scoring and evidence URLs, then let Ava act on it automatically."}],"blogName":"Artisan vs Unify: which fits your team?"}},"heroImage":{"url":"https://images.ctfassets.net/kyprwggh4muz/7oNTRRsVhtEKH3wpGJ2Lg9/1955d7652a40f02e0f1772978cb43881/artisan-vs-unify-cover.webp","width":2389,"height":1120,"title":"Artisan vs Unify: which fits your team in 2026?"},"content":{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Both Artisan and Unify start from signals: the buying moments that tell you who to reach. Unify is a warm-outbound system of action that aggregates signals and fires automated plays your ops team configures. Artisan turns signals into fully-run outreach: Ava, an AI BDR, catches the trigger and runs the campaign herself. The split is who operates the machine.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Which one fits your situation?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Your situation","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Better fit","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You have a RevOps team that enjoys building and tuning signal plays","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Unify","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You want signals to trigger fully-run outreach without an operator","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Artisan","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You want a low-cost, seat-based entry point to test warm outbound","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Unify","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You want data, enrichment, calling, and reply handling in one platform","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Artisan","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You're layering signal plays on top of an existing outbound stack","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Unify","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You're consolidating a 5-8 tool stack into one AI-run system","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Artisan","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You measure success by play sophistication and signal coverage","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Unify","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You measure success by booked meetings without added headcount","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Artisan","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"}],"nodeType":"table"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Prospecting: catching the signal","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Unify is strong at the signal layer. It aggregates website visitor data, intent, and buying signals, then feeds them into automated sequences, which is why signal-led teams like it. If your motion is \"watch for the right moment, then reach out warm,\" Unify gives you a clean system to build that on.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{"target":{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"kyprwggh4muz"}},"id":"61fQTFyhcOoMqizz5RJIOS","type":"Asset","createdAt":"2026-09-20T01:39:08.933Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-20T01:39:08.933Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":2,"revision":1,"locale":"en-US"},"fields":{"title":"Artisan vs Unify key points","description":"Infographic for the Artisan vs Unify comparison","file":{"url":"//images.ctfassets.net/kyprwggh4muz/61fQTFyhcOoMqizz5RJIOS/b8bb2ee325cca7de6e779b027d951c7a/artisan-vs-unify-infographic.png","details":{"size":103969,"image":{"width":1080,"height":1080}},"fileName":"artisan-vs-unify-infographic.png","contentType":"image/png"}}}},"content":[],"nodeType":"embedded-asset-block"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Artisan covers the same signal surface and then some, natively. Its signals include funding rounds, recently hired executives, first hire in a department, actively hiring for a role, tech-stack intent, Bombora-powered topic intent, social post keyword tracking, champion job-change tracking, investor portfolio tracking, and website visitor identification. It also supports natural-language custom AI signals: describe any trigger in plain English and Ava scores it with confidence and evidence URLs. The database behind it spans over 250 million B2B professionals across over 200 countries, plus Artisan Local Data with over 250 million local businesses. So the signal and the enriched, ready-to-contact record arrive together.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The difference isn't whether each catches signals. Both do. It's what happens the instant a signal fires.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Activation: does the signal trigger a play or a worker?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Here's the real distinction. When a signal fires in Unify, it triggers an automated play that your ops team designed: the sequence, the copy, the branching logic, the maintenance. Unify runs the play well, but the intelligence is front-loaded into how a human configured it. It's a system of action, and a person is the system's architect and operator.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"When a signal fires in Artisan, it triggers Ava. She enriches the lead, writes personalized messaging per contact rather than a shared template, sends across email and social outreach, dials the call steps for a rep to take over, runs dozens of message variations, and shifts volume toward what converts. Two leads that hit the same trigger get two completely different messages. You didn't build the play; the AI runs the motion and adapts it. That's the gap between an ops-configured engine and an AI employee.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"It's also the consolidation case. A typical outbound stack runs 5-8 tools at $100K+/year plus the headcount to operate them. Artisan folds the signals, data, enrichment, copywriting, sending, and reply handling into one platform an AI runs.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Booking meetings: who works the reply?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Unify's automated plays send outreach, but the reply handling and booking lean on your team and connected tools. The play gets the message out; a human generally takes it from there.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Ava handles every reply. She qualifies leads, answers objections from a knowledge base you control, chases follow-ups, and books meetings on reps' calendars with CRM-owner routing so the meeting lands with the right rep. Escalation runs on plain-language rules you write, so a person steps in exactly when you want. The signal-to-meeting loop closes inside one system, without a rep watching the inbox, which is what \"fully-run outreach\" actually means.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Pricing: seats plus credits vs pay for work performed","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Unify's pricing has come down and opened up. Its public tiers now start at Free for up to 3 seats, Base at $20/seat/month, and Pro at $60/seat/month, with Business custom, plus usage credits on top. That's an accessible entry point, and the old ~$700/month framing no longer applies. The real cost, as with any ops-configured system, includes the team time to build and tune the plays.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Artisan is usage-based: you pay for work performed rather than per seat, and there is no per-seat platform fee. Calling is built into the platform rather than sold as a separate per-seat dialer. The full model is at ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/pricing"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"https://www.artisan.co/pricing","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":". The comparison to make isn't seat price alone; it's seats-plus-operator-time versus an AI that runs the motion.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Governance and enterprise fit","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Both can serve growing teams; Unify has strong signal-led logos and a healthy Series B behind it. Artisan is built for scale on the governance side: SOC 2 Type II, with SSO, SAML, role-based access using built-in and custom roles, and a full audit trail. Large teams commonly run Ava centrally from sales ops for AEs who never log in, and the autonomy dial lets you keep review-and-approve control while the AI does the work. The Enterprise plan adds a forward-deployed strategist and a dedicated CSM.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"A customer data point on fully-run outreach. Amelia Lerutte, Chief AI Officer at SaaStr, said: \"Email has always been our number one driver. Artisan is now neck-and-neck in both output and closed-won revenue.\" SaaStr sent 6,892 emails at a 3.6% positive response rate in about six weeks. That's signals and sends running at volume without a team hand-tuning every play.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Choose Unify if","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You have a RevOps or growth-engineering function that enjoys designing and iterating on signal-based plays and wants control over each one.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You want a low-cost, seat-based entry point to test warm outbound before committing to a fuller platform.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You're layering signal-triggered sequences on top of an outbound stack you already like, rather than consolidating it.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Your team's edge is the sophistication of your plays, and you'd rather build that yourself than hand it to an AI.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"}],"nodeType":"unordered-list"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"If that's you, Unify is a capable signal-driven system and a fair pick. Artisan wins when you want signals to trigger outreach that an AI actually runs, enrichment through booking, without staffing the operator role.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Frequently asked questions","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Is Unify better than Artisan for signal-based outbound?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Unify is a strong signal aggregator and play engine, and if you want to design the plays yourself, it does that well. Artisan covers the same signals, including natural-language custom triggers with confidence scoring, and then runs the outreach itself rather than executing a play your ops team configured. If you want control over each play, Unify; if you want the signal to trigger a worker, Artisan.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"How much does Unify cost now?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Unify's public pricing starts at Free for up to 3 seats, Base at $20/seat/month, and Pro at $60/seat/month, with Business custom, plus usage credits. The frequently cited ~$700/month figure is obsolete. Artisan is usage-based: you pay for work performed, not seats. Compare total cost including the team time each model requires to operate.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Does Artisan replace Unify?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"For teams whose Unify usage is signal-triggered outbound, generally yes, because Artisan detects the signals, enriches the leads, runs the multichannel outreach, handles replies, and books meetings in one platform. Unify remains a fit for teams that want to build and own their own plays on top of an existing stack. The core difference is ops-configured plays versus an AI that runs the motion.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Can Artisan create custom signals like Unify?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Yes, and it goes further with natural-language custom signals: define any trigger in plain English, and Ava scores it with confidence and evidence URLs, then acts on it automatically. Alongside those, Artisan tracks funding rounds, new executive hires, hiring activity, tech-stack and topic intent, champion job changes, and website visitors. The signal fires and Ava runs the outreach, rather than handing off to a configured play.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Is Unify enterprise-ready?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Unify is a well-funded, capable platform used by notable teams, and it scales for signal-led motions. Artisan carries a broader enterprise governance posture out of the box: SOC 2 Type II, SSO, SAML, role-based access, and a central-ops deployment pattern with a full audit trail. Which matters more depends on whether you need the plays or the governed, AI-run motion.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Which gets to booked meetings faster?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Artisan typically closes the signal-to-meeting loop faster because reply handling and booking are built in and run by Ava, with CRM-owner routing. Unify's plays send outreach effectively, but qualification and booking usually lean on your team downstream. If speed from trigger to meeting without added headcount is the goal, Artisan is the shorter loop.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The bottom line","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Unify is a capable warm-outbound system of action, and for teams that want to design their own signal plays at an accessible entry price, it's a reasonable choice. Artisan is for teams that want signals to trigger outreach an AI actually runs: over 250 million B2B professionals across over 200 countries, plus Artisan Local Data with over 250 million local businesses, native and natural-language signals, and an AI BDR who takes it from trigger to booked meeting, as autonomously as you want.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"See Ava work on the ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"Artisan homepage","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":", read the ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/blog/ai-bdr"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"AI BDR guide","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":", explore the ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/ai-sales-agent"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"AI sales agent","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":", or review the ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/pricing"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"pricing model","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":". Comparing enterprise ABM tools? See ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/blog/artisan-vs-6sense"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"Artisan vs 6sense","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":".","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"document"},"authors":[{"id":"2BNzbXmPpTiXXI35GfMMwO","slug":"jaspar-carmichael-jack","authorName":"Jaspar Carmichael-Jack","authorDesignation":"Co-Founder & CEO @ Artisan","authorDescription":"Jaspar is an entrepreneur with expertise in sales, marketing, and operations. He founded Artisan in 2023, a company automating workflows with AI employees.","profileImageUrl":"https://ca.slack-edge.com/T05QXKPJQNN-U05RMB3DP1N-83c0c4161322-512","authorSocials":{"twitter":"https://x.com/jasparcjack","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jaspar-carmichael-jack"}}],"fields":{"blogNavigation":{"fields":{"contentNavigation":[{"label":"Which one fits your situation?","link":"#which_one_fits_your_situation?"},{"label":"Prospecting: catching the signal","link":"#prospecting_catching_the_signal"},{"label":"Activation: does the signal trigger a play or a worker?","link":"#activation_does_the_signal_trigger_a_play_or_a_worker?"},{"label":"Booking meetings: who works the reply?","link":"#booking_meetings_who_works_the_reply?"},{"label":"Pricing: seats plus credits vs pay for work performed","link":"#pricing_seats_plus_credits_vs_pay_for_work_performed"},{"label":"Governance and enterprise fit","link":"#governance_and_enterprise_fit"},{"label":"Choose Unify if","link":"#choose_unify_if"},{"label":"Frequently asked questions","link":"#frequently_asked_questions"},{"label":"The bottom line","link":"#the_bottom_line"}]}}}},{"id":"3PxQltfOM2uIHCu9b4w6QY","slug":"salesloft-vs-hubspot-sales-hub-which-should-you-choose","title":"Salesloft vs HubSpot Sales Hub: which should you choose in 2026?","metaTitle":"Salesloft vs HubSpot Sales Hub: which to choose in 2026?","publishedDate":"2026-09-17","seoDescription":"An honest 2026 comparison of Salesloft and HubSpot Sales Hub across CRM fit, cadence governance, Breeze credit-based pricing, and the Clari merger.","readTime":"7 minutes","tag":"Sales","keyTakeAways":{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"kyprwggh4muz"}},"id":"1x1GNHPfiLVmr3mvVPQykh","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-09-17T04:31:47.595Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-17T04:31:47.595Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":1,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"blogKeyTakeaways"}},"locale":"en-US"},"fields":{"keyTakeAways":[{"keyTakeAways":"HubSpot Sales Hub is native to the HubSpot CRM, so contacts, deals, sequences, and reporting live on one record; its value peaks when your whole motion already runs on HubSpot."},{"keyTakeAways":"HubSpot's Breeze agents bill through bundled HubSpot Credits at about $0.010 per credit, a usage-based model that ties AI cost to consumption rather than seats."},{"keyTakeAways":"Salesloft is a dedicated, CRM-agnostic engagement platform with mature cadence governance, now paired with Clari forecasting after the merger closed December 3, 2025."},{"keyTakeAways":"Salesloft's deeper cadence controls suit large, disciplined orgs; Sales Hub's strength is that it sits on the CRM your team already lives in, with credit-based Breeze agents attached."},{"keyTakeAways":"Both keep a human rep driving the outreach; the AI in each assists rather than runs the motion end to end."}],"blogName":"Salesloft vs HubSpot Sales Hub: which should you choose in 2026?"}},"heroImage":{"url":"https://images.ctfassets.net/kyprwggh4muz/1UKZ9WtoBAZw9nhpEu4thT/a16115e7c75182bcb66e94f984fe08a9/salesloft-vs-hubspot-cover.webp","width":2389,"height":1120,"title":"Salesloft vs HubSpot Sales Hub: which should you choose in 2026?"},"content":{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Salesloft and HubSpot Sales Hub both run cadences, but the deciding factor is your CRM. Sales Hub is native to HubSpot, so everything lives on one record, and its Breeze agents now bill through bundled HubSpot Credits at about $0.010 per credit, a usage-based model rather than a per-seat AI charge. Salesloft is a dedicated engagement platform, CRM-agnostic, now paired with Clari forecasting after the December 2025 merger.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"These two rarely land on the same shortlist by accident. Teams already committed to HubSpot compare Sales Hub against a specialist engagement tool like Salesloft to decide whether native convenience beats dedicated depth. Teams that are CRM-agnostic weigh Salesloft's cadence maturity against HubSpot's single-record simplicity and its new pricing model. This comparison lays out both fairly so you can match the tool to your stack.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"How Salesloft and HubSpot Sales Hub compare","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Salesloft","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"HubSpot Sales Hub","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Best for","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Large orgs wanting dedicated cadence plus forecasting","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Teams whose motion already runs on HubSpot","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"CRM fit","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"CRM-agnostic, integrates broadly","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Native to HubSpot, single-record model","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Cadence governance","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Mature, deep controls for large teams","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Solid within the HubSpot ecosystem","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Forecasting","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Native via the Clari merger (Dec 2025)","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Within HubSpot reporting","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"AI pricing","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Standard per-seat model","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Breeze via bundled HubSpot Credits, ~$0.010/credit","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Public pricing","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Not published; enterprise sales-led","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Published per-seat tiers, per its pricing page","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"}],"nodeType":"table"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"What is the core difference between Salesloft and Sales Hub?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"It comes down to where your data lives. HubSpot Sales Hub is part of the HubSpot platform, so cadences, contacts, deals, and reporting all sit on the same record. There is no sync layer to manage because there is nothing to sync; the engagement tool and the CRM are one system. That is its biggest advantage and also its boundary: the value is highest inside HubSpot and thins outside it.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{"target":{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"kyprwggh4muz"}},"id":"6tFKrddiWhuG6Y77aOK8JG","type":"Asset","createdAt":"2026-09-17T03:40:28.415Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-17T03:40:28.415Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":2,"revision":1,"locale":"en-US"},"fields":{"title":"Salesloft vs HubSpot Sales Hub infographic","description":"Infographic for the Salesloft vs HubSpot Sales Hub article","file":{"url":"//images.ctfassets.net/kyprwggh4muz/6tFKrddiWhuG6Y77aOK8JG/2a3f7bdeeb3b9152a1a8881e2fe0bad4/salesloft-vs-hubspot-sales-hub-infographic.png","details":{"size":111147,"image":{"width":1080,"height":1080}},"fileName":"salesloft-vs-hubspot-sales-hub-infographic.png","contentType":"image/png"}}}},"content":[],"nodeType":"embedded-asset-block"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Salesloft is a standalone engagement platform designed to work across CRMs. It brings deeper, more specialized cadence governance and, since the December 2025 Clari merger, native forecasting. You run it alongside your CRM rather than inside one. So the choice is native convenience versus dedicated depth, and your existing CRM commitment usually settles it.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Which is better if you already run HubSpot?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"If your entire motion already lives in HubSpot, Sales Hub is the natural pick. Everything stays on one record, there is no integration to maintain, and reps work cadences in the same place they manage deals. Adding a separate engagement platform on top of HubSpot means paying for and maintaining a tool that duplicates part of what you already own, which only makes sense if you need governance depth HubSpot cannot match.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The counterpoint is scope. Sales Hub's advantage is strongest inside the HubSpot world and weaker for teams with a mixed stack or a Salesforce core. If HubSpot is your system of record and you value single-record simplicity, Sales Hub wins this scenario clearly. If you are CRM-agnostic or on Salesforce, the native advantage disappears and Salesloft's depth becomes more relevant.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Which has deeper cadence governance?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Salesloft. It is a dedicated engagement platform built for large, disciplined sales orgs, with mature sequence controls, team permissions, and reporting depth honed over years as a category specialist. When an organization has many reps and needs strict process enforcement, Salesloft's governance is the more specialized answer.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Sales Hub's cadence tools are solid and well integrated, though engagement is one part of a broad CRM platform. For a mid-market team running its motion on HubSpot, that depth is usually enough. For a large org whose priority is tight cadence governance above all, Salesloft's specialization shows. Match the depth to how demanding your process control actually is.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"How does HubSpot's Breeze pricing work?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"HubSpot's Breeze agents bill through bundled HubSpot Credits at roughly $0.010 per credit, a usage-based model worth citing because it ties AI cost to consumption rather than to a seat. That reframed the buying question for a lot of teams: instead of asking only what a license costs, they started asking how much AI work they will actually run and what those credits add up to.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"For a Sales Hub buyer, it means the AI agent layer scales with usage rather than headcount, which is appealing if you want cost to track how much the agents do. Salesloft, by contrast, uses a standard per-seat enterprise model. Neither approach is automatically better; credit-based usage rewards teams that can forecast their consumption, while per-seat pricing is predictable regardless of volume. The point is that HubSpot's move made the pricing question sharper across the whole category.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"What did the Salesloft and Clari merger change?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The merger closed December 3, 2025, combining Salesloft's cadence with Clari's forecasting under one company. For a buyer who wants engagement and forecasting from the same vendor, that is a real draw and a clear differentiator against Sales Hub, whose forecasting lives inside HubSpot's own reporting.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The trade-off is roadmap uncertainty common to large mergers. New buyers should ask where the combined product is headed and how the two sides integrate over time. Those are fair questions for a sales conversation. If forecasting tied to cadence is central to your motion and you are comfortable with post-merger questions, the combined Salesloft-Clari story is a point in its favor.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"A third option to know about","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Both tools keep a human rep running the motion: whichever you pick, Sales Hub gives reps assistive agents inside HubSpot and Salesloft organizes what reps do next, but the rep still writes, sends, calls, and replies. Their AI assists that person rather than replacing the work.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"If you would rather the software do the outbound work rather than assist with it, an autonomous platform is a third path. ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"Artisan","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" built Ava, an ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/ai-sales-agent"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"autonomous AI sales agent","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":", to run the outbound motion: she sources, writes, sends, replies, and books on her own, with calling built in. On call steps, she dials and a rep handles the live conversation. Ava runs on usage-based pricing. That is a different purchase from a cadence tool you staff and drive, and it fits teams that want the outcome rather than a better console for reps. Our guide to ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/blog/the-best-sales-engagement-platforms"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"the best sales engagement platforms","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" maps where each model fits.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Choose Salesloft if","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You want a dedicated engagement platform with deep cadence governance for a large team.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Your stack is CRM-agnostic or Salesforce-centric rather than HubSpot-native.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Forecasting tied to cadence, via the Clari merger, is central to your motion.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Process control across many reps outweighs single-record convenience.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You are comfortable with an enterprise, sales-led purchase and post-merger roadmap questions.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"}],"nodeType":"unordered-list"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Choose HubSpot Sales Hub if","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Your entire motion already runs on HubSpot and you value one record for everything.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You want no integration layer between engagement and CRM.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Breeze billed through bundled HubSpot Credits at about $0.010 per credit fits how you want to buy AI.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Your cadence needs are well served by solid, integrated controls rather than specialist depth.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Published, self-serve pricing matters more than dedicated enterprise governance.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"}],"nodeType":"unordered-list"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Frequently asked questions","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Is HubSpot Sales Hub or Salesloft better?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"It depends on your CRM. If your motion already runs on HubSpot, Sales Hub keeps everything on one record with no integration to maintain, and its Breeze agents bill through bundled HubSpot Credits at about $0.010 per credit. Salesloft is the better pick for CRM-agnostic or Salesforce-centric teams that need deeper, specialist cadence governance and want forecasting tied to cadence via the Clari merger. Match the tool to your stack.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"How is HubSpot's Breeze pricing structured?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"HubSpot's Breeze agents bill through bundled HubSpot Credits at roughly $0.010 per credit, a usage-based model that ties AI cost to consumption rather than to a seat. It appeals to teams that want cost to track how much the agents actually do and can forecast that usage. Salesloft, by contrast, uses a standard per-seat enterprise model. Neither is automatically better; credit-based usage and per-seat pricing suit different buying preferences.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Do I need Salesloft if I already use HubSpot?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Usually not, unless you need governance depth HubSpot cannot match. Sales Hub already provides cadences inside the CRM, so adding Salesloft means paying for and maintaining a tool that duplicates part of that. The case for running Salesloft alongside HubSpot is a large, disciplined org that needs Salesloft's specialist cadence controls. For most HubSpot-native teams, Sales Hub is enough.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"How does the Salesloft and Clari merger affect the choice?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The merger, closed December 3, 2025, adds native forecasting to Salesloft's cadence, which Sales Hub answers with HubSpot's own reporting. If forecasting tied to cadence from one vendor matters to you, that favors Salesloft. The trade-off is roadmap uncertainty typical of large mergers, so ask where the combined product is headed before committing. It is a differentiator with a caveat attached.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"How much do Salesloft and HubSpot Sales Hub cost?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"HubSpot Sales Hub publishes per-seat tiers on its pricing page (Free, Starter, Professional, and Enterprise), and its Breeze agents bill through bundled HubSpot Credits at about $0.010 per credit. Salesloft does not publish self-serve pricing; its numbers come through an enterprise sales process and depend on volume and term. So Sales Hub offers more pricing transparency up front, while Salesloft is a quoted enterprise purchase.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Is there an alternative to both Salesloft and HubSpot Sales Hub?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Yes. Both keep a human rep driving: Sales Hub gives reps assistive Breeze agents inside HubSpot and Salesloft prompts what reps do next, but the reps still write, send, call, and reply. If you want the software to execute the outbound job itself, Artisan's Ava is an ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/ai-sales-agent"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"autonomous AI sales agent","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" that sources, writes, sends, replies, and books on her own, with calling built in. On call steps, she dials and a rep handles the live conversation. It runs on usage-based pricing, a different category than an engagement tool, suited to teams that want the motion owned end to end rather than orchestrated for reps.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"document"},"authors":[{"id":"2BNzbXmPpTiXXI35GfMMwO","slug":"jaspar-carmichael-jack","authorName":"Jaspar Carmichael-Jack","authorDesignation":"Co-Founder & CEO @ Artisan","authorDescription":"Jaspar is an entrepreneur with expertise in sales, marketing, and operations. He founded Artisan in 2023, a company automating workflows with AI employees.","profileImageUrl":"https://ca.slack-edge.com/T05QXKPJQNN-U05RMB3DP1N-83c0c4161322-512","authorSocials":{"twitter":"https://x.com/jasparcjack","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jaspar-carmichael-jack"}}],"fields":{"blogNavigation":{"fields":{"contentNavigation":[{"label":"How Salesloft and HubSpot Sales Hub compare","link":"#how_salesloft_and_hubspot_sales_hub_compare"},{"label":"What is the core difference between Salesloft and Sales Hub?","link":"#what_is_the_core_difference_between_salesloft_and_sales_hub?"},{"label":"Which is better if you already run HubSpot?","link":"#which_is_better_if_you_already_run_hubspot?"},{"label":"Which has deeper cadence governance?","link":"#which_has_deeper_cadence_governance?"},{"label":"How does HubSpot's Breeze pricing work?","link":"#how_does_hubspots_breeze_pricing_work?"},{"label":"What did the Salesloft and Clari merger change?","link":"#what_did_the_salesloft_and_clari_merger_change?"},{"label":"A third option to know about","link":"#a_third_option_to_know_about"},{"label":"Choose Salesloft if","link":"#choose_salesloft_if"},{"label":"Choose HubSpot Sales Hub if","link":"#choose_hubspot_sales_hub_if"},{"label":"Frequently asked questions","link":"#frequently_asked_questions"}]}}}},{"id":"gHZBjT2H8dKCUw85pQOnE","slug":"outreach-vs-salesloft-which-should-you-choose","title":"Outreach vs Salesloft: which should you choose in 2026?","metaTitle":"Outreach vs Salesloft: which should you choose in 2026?","publishedDate":"2026-09-17","seoDescription":"An honest 2026 comparison of Outreach and Salesloft after the Clari merger, across cadence, forecasting, AI, stability, and pricing.","readTime":"7 minutes","tag":"Sales","keyTakeAways":{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"kyprwggh4muz"}},"id":"19UGFRINB9944VpZYR8Asx","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-09-17T04:31:47.567Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-17T04:31:47.567Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":1,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"blogKeyTakeaways"}},"locale":"en-US"},"fields":{"keyTakeAways":[{"keyTakeAways":"Salesloft merged with Clari, closing December 3, 2025, pairing enterprise cadence with forecasting under one company but leaving new buyers with post-merger roadmap questions."},{"keyTakeAways":"Outreach remained independent and added its Omni agent in April 2026 to bring more AI into the sequencing flow; its pricing is not public, with reported figures around $100 to $160 per user per month (an estimate)."},{"keyTakeAways":"Both platforms are human-driven: they orchestrate what reps do next rather than executing the outreach themselves."},{"keyTakeAways":"Salesloft's former sibling product Drift suffered a 2025 supply-chain breach reported by Google threat intelligence, and its retirement was announced in March 2026; the two are separate products, but it is worth knowing."},{"keyTakeAways":"Cadence governance is close to a tie; the tiebreakers are forecasting (Salesloft plus Clari) versus product stability and independence (Outreach)."}],"blogName":"Outreach vs Salesloft: which should you choose in 2026?"}},"heroImage":{"url":"https://images.ctfassets.net/kyprwggh4muz/7JAUwjM5jFlql9zGRwarwm/23bca5a63821d2f1d830cc7f2eae47d8/outreach-vs-salesloft-cover.webp","width":2389,"height":1120,"title":"Outreach vs Salesloft: which should you choose in 2026?"},"content":{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Outreach and Salesloft are the two enterprise sales engagement incumbents, and they are more alike than different: mature cadence governance, deep CRM sync, and reporting built for large orgs. The 2026 decision hinges on two things. Salesloft closed a merger with Clari on December 3, 2025, adding forecasting but raising roadmap questions. Outreach stayed independent.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"For years these were the default two-tool shortlist for any enterprise buying sales engagement. The core capability, running disciplined multichannel cadences that tell reps what to do next, is close to a tie. What separates them now is corporate direction: Salesloft's move into a combined cadence-plus-forecasting company, and Outreach's steadier, standalone path with its own AI agent. This comparison weighs both fairly.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"How Outreach and Salesloft compare","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Outreach","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Salesloft","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Best for","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Teams wanting a stable, independent enterprise sequencer","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Teams that want cadence and forecasting from one company","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Cadence governance","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Mature, deep sequence and permission controls","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Mature, built for large disciplined orgs","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Forecasting","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Not native; pairs with separate tools","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Native via the Clari merger (closed Dec 2025)","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"AI layer","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Omni agent (added Apr 2026)","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"AI features within a human-driven cadence","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Corporate status","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Independent","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Merged with Clari, December 3, 2025","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Public pricing","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Not public; around $100 to $160/user/mo (estimated, low confidence)","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Not public; estimated around $125 to $165/user/mo (low confidence), dialer add-on extra","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"}],"nodeType":"table"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"What is the difference between Outreach and Salesloft?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"At the feature level, less than most buyers expect. Both run multichannel cadences across email, calls, and social outreach, both enforce process across large rep teams, and both sync deeply with the CRM and report on activity. If you put the two cadence builders side by side, an experienced ops leader would find them comparably capable.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{"target":{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"kyprwggh4muz"}},"id":"2by6vvxuW57XPUEyH31nfp","type":"Asset","createdAt":"2026-09-17T03:40:28.413Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-17T03:40:28.413Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":2,"revision":1,"locale":"en-US"},"fields":{"title":"Outreach vs Salesloft infographic","description":"Infographic for the Outreach vs Salesloft article","file":{"url":"//images.ctfassets.net/kyprwggh4muz/2by6vvxuW57XPUEyH31nfp/e94a828c026c73c4abac0d55002a9a9e/outreach-vs-salesloft-infographic.png","details":{"size":104325,"image":{"width":1080,"height":1080}},"fileName":"outreach-vs-salesloft-infographic.png","contentType":"image/png"}}}},"content":[],"nodeType":"embedded-asset-block"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The difference is strategic. Salesloft is now part of a combined company with Clari, so its story is cadence plus forecasting from a single vendor. Outreach is a focused, independent sales engagement platform that added its own AI agent rather than a forecasting suite. So the real question is not which sequencer is better, it is which corporate bet fits your roadmap and your appetite for change.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Which has better cadence and workflow governance?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"This is close to a tie, and that is the honest answer. Both were built for large, disciplined sales organizations and both offer deep sequence controls, team permissions, and step-level reporting. Neither has a governance gap the other exploits. Teams that have run both tend to describe the choice as a matter of taste and existing integrations rather than a capability gap.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Outreach edges slightly ahead on being a single-focus product: its entire roadmap goes into engagement. Salesloft's attention is now split across a broader cadence-and-forecasting platform. Whether that is a plus or a minus depends on whether you value forecasting integration or focused engagement investment. On raw cadence governance alone, treat them as even and let the tiebreakers decide.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"What did the Salesloft and Clari merger change?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The merger closed December 3, 2025, combining Salesloft's cadence with Clari's forecasting and revenue analytics under one roof. For a buyer who wants execution and forecasting from the same vendor, that is a genuine draw, and it is Salesloft's clearest differentiator against Outreach right now. For background, Vista Equity Partners recapitalized Salesloft in 2022 in a deal reported at around $2.3 billion.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The flip side is uncertainty. Any merger this size leaves new buyers unsure where the combined product is headed, which features get prioritized, and how integrations evolve. Those are fair questions to raise in a sales conversation. Separately, Salesloft's former sibling product Drift suffered a 2025 supply-chain breach reported by Google threat intelligence, and its retirement was announced in March 2026. Drift is a distinct product from Salesloft's core engagement platform, but the history is worth knowing when you evaluate the wider portfolio.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Which is better for forecasting?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Salesloft, because of the Clari merger. If you want your cadence platform and your forecasting to come from the same company, with tighter integration between rep activity and revenue prediction, the combined Salesloft-Clari entity is built for exactly that. That is the strongest single reason to pick Salesloft over Outreach in 2026.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Outreach does not ship native forecasting in the same way. Teams using Outreach typically pair it with a separate forecasting tool. If forecasting is central to how you run the business and you would rather not stitch two vendors together, Salesloft's combined story wins this category outright.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"How do they compare on price?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Both are enterprise purchases sold through a sales process, not self-serve, and neither publishes pricing. Outreach's reported figures sit around $100 to $160 per user per month (an estimate, low confidence), often with implementation fees estimated at roughly $5,000 to $25,000. Salesloft's numbers come through negotiation; third-party estimates put it around $125 to $165 per user per month (low confidence), with its dialer typically an add-on billed separately.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Because both are quoted rather than listed, the real number depends on volume, term, and what modules you take. With Salesloft, factor in the forecasting side of the combined platform; with Outreach, factor in the separate forecasting tool you may need. Price is unlikely to be the deciding factor between these two; fit and stability are.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"A third option to know about","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Both tools share one structural limit: whichever you pick, they tell a rep what to do next, and the rep still writes, sends, calls, and replies. Their AI features assist that person rather than replace the work. If what you actually want is the software to do more of the work rather than schedule it, an AI-driven platform is a third path.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"Artisan","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" built Ava, an ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/ai-sales-agent"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"AI sales agent","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" (an AI BDR for outbound), to run much of the motion herself: she sources contacts, writes and sends outreach, and handles replies. Calling is built in: she dials the call steps and a rep handles the live conversation. Pricing is usage-based rather than per seat, with no platform fee, and Ava can be trialled for free. That is a different purchase from a sequencer you staff and drive, and it fits teams that want the outcome rather than a better console for reps. Our guide to ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/blog/the-best-sales-engagement-platforms"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"the best sales engagement platforms","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" covers where each model fits.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Choose Outreach if","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You want a stable, independent enterprise sequencer without merger uncertainty.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Deep cadence governance and process control across many reps is your priority.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You already have or prefer a separate forecasting tool.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You want a focused engagement product whose full roadmap goes into that job.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The Omni agent inside a mature platform is the AI story you want.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"}],"nodeType":"unordered-list"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Choose Salesloft if","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You want cadence and forecasting from one vendor, via the Clari merger.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Tight integration between rep activity and revenue prediction matters to your motion.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You are comfortable with post-merger roadmap questions in exchange for that combined platform.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Your enterprise process needs mature, disciplined cadence governance, which Salesloft matches.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"You value the broader revenue-operations story the combined company tells.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"list-item"}],"nodeType":"unordered-list"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Frequently asked questions","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Are Outreach and Salesloft basically the same?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"On core cadence capability, they are close. Both run disciplined multichannel sequences, enforce process across large teams, and sync deeply with the CRM. The meaningful differences are corporate: Salesloft merged with Clari on December 3, 2025 to add forecasting, while Outreach stayed independent and added its Omni agent in April 2026. Choose based on whether you want combined forecasting or a focused, independent engagement platform.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"What does the Salesloft and Clari merger mean for buyers?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The merger, closed December 3, 2025, pairs Salesloft's cadence with Clari's forecasting under one company, which is a real draw if you want both from one vendor. The trade-off is roadmap uncertainty common to large mergers: it is fair to ask which features get prioritized and how integrations evolve. Raise those questions directly in a sales conversation before committing to a multi-year term.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Is Salesloft affected by the Drift breach?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Drift, a former sibling product, suffered a 2025 supply-chain breach reported by Google threat intelligence, and its retirement was announced in March 2026. Drift is a separate product from Salesloft's core sales engagement platform, so the breach is not a direct statement about the cadence tool. It is still reasonable to review the vendor's overall security posture and portfolio history as part of your evaluation.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Which has better forecasting, Outreach or Salesloft?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Salesloft, because of the Clari merger. It offers native forecasting and revenue analytics tied to cadence activity from the same company. Outreach does not ship equivalent native forecasting; teams typically pair it with a separate tool. If forecasting integration is central to how you run the business, that is the clearest reason to choose Salesloft over Outreach.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"How much do Outreach and Salesloft cost?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Neither publishes public pricing. Outreach's reported figures are around $100 to $160 per user per month (an estimate), typically with implementation fees, sold through an enterprise process. Salesloft's numbers come through negotiation; third-party estimates put it around $125 to $165 per user per month, with the dialer usually an add-on, and you should factor in the forecasting side of the combined platform. Neither is a self-serve purchase, so expect a quote based on volume and term.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Is there an alternative to both Outreach and Salesloft?","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-3"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Yes. Both Outreach and Salesloft are human-driven engagement platforms: they organize and prompt what reps do next, but the reps still write, send, call, and reply. If you want the software to run more of the motion itself, Artisan's Ava is an ","nodeType":"text"},{"data":{"uri":"https://www.artisan.co/ai-sales-agent"},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"value":"AI sales agent","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"hyperlink"},{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":" (AI BDR) that sources contacts, writes and sends outreach, and handles replies, priced on usage rather than per seat. Calling is built in: she dials the call steps and a rep handles the live conversation. It is a different category from a sequencer, suited to teams that want the motion owned end to end rather than orchestrated for reps.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"document"},"authors":[{"id":"2BNzbXmPpTiXXI35GfMMwO","slug":"jaspar-carmichael-jack","authorName":"Jaspar Carmichael-Jack","authorDesignation":"Co-Founder & CEO @ Artisan","authorDescription":"Jaspar is an entrepreneur with expertise in sales, marketing, and operations. He founded Artisan in 2023, a company automating workflows with AI employees.","profileImageUrl":"https://ca.slack-edge.com/T05QXKPJQNN-U05RMB3DP1N-83c0c4161322-512","authorSocials":{"twitter":"https://x.com/jasparcjack","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jaspar-carmichael-jack"}}],"fields":{"blogNavigation":{"fields":{"contentNavigation":[{"label":"How Outreach and Salesloft compare","link":"#how_outreach_and_salesloft_compare"},{"label":"What is the difference between Outreach and Salesloft?","link":"#what_is_the_difference_between_outreach_and_salesloft?"},{"label":"Which has better cadence and workflow governance?","link":"#which_has_better_cadence_and_workflow_governance?"},{"label":"What did the Salesloft and Clari merger change?","link":"#what_did_the_salesloft_and_clari_merger_change?"},{"label":"Which is better for forecasting?","link":"#which_is_better_for_forecasting?"},{"label":"How do they compare on price?","link":"#how_do_they_compare_on_price?"},{"label":"A third option to know about","link":"#a_third_option_to_know_about"},{"label":"Choose Outreach if","link":"#choose_outreach_if"},{"label":"Choose Salesloft if","link":"#choose_salesloft_if"},{"label":"Frequently asked questions","link":"#frequently_asked_questions"}]}}}},{"id":"5yR5EFnKwSaNctpTkry09e","slug":"the-best-salesforce-sales-engagement-alternatives","title":"The best Salesforce Sales Engagement alternatives in 2026","metaTitle":"Best Salesforce Sales Engagement alternatives 2026","publishedDate":"2026-09-17","seoDescription":"The best Salesforce Sales Engagement alternatives in 2026, from an autonomous AI BDR to Outreach, Salesloft, HubSpot, Apollo, and Groove.","readTime":"9 minutes","tag":"Sales","keyTakeAways":{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"kyprwggh4muz"}},"id":"57v3OYK7zxO6sDJ6AgeWAN","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-09-17T04:31:47.535Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-17T04:31:47.535Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":1,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"blogKeyTakeaways"}},"locale":"en-US"},"fields":{"keyTakeAways":[{"keyTakeAways":"Salesforce Sales Engagement is powerful but heavy: setup, admin, and configuration usually need dedicated ops resource to run well."},{"keyTakeAways":"It works the contacts already in Salesforce rather than sourcing net-new prospects at scale."},{"keyTakeAways":"Agentforce SDR pricing is consumption-based and evolving, $2 per conversation, or $0.10 per standard action on Flex Credits."},{"keyTakeAways":"Artisan replaces the configure-for-reps model with Ava, an autonomous AI BDR who sources net-new and runs the motion under a set autonomy level, with deep two-way Salesforce sync."},{"keyTakeAways":"Outreach and Salesloft are the mature engagement specialists; Groove is the Salesforce-native third-party option."},{"keyTakeAways":"Autonomy is a dial from review-and-approve to fully autonomous, with escalation rules and a full audit trail."}],"blogName":"The best Salesforce Sales Engagement alternatives in 2026"}},"heroImage":{"url":"https://images.ctfassets.net/kyprwggh4muz/27VRuFC7fpIR77xxzGU4DS/443e8fed71aac39e05b15876d8ed4faf/the-best-salesforce-sales-engagement-alternatives-cover.png","width":2389,"height":1120,"title":"The best Salesforce Sales Engagement alternatives in 2026"},"content":{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The best Salesforce Sales Engagement alternative is Artisan: instead of configuring a heavy native cadence tool for reps, Ava runs the motion herself, sourcing net-new leads, writing, sending, replying, and booking, and dialing the call steps with a rep taking the live conversation. Outreach and Salesloft are the mature specialists, HubSpot fits HubSpot shops, Apollo bundles data cheaply, and Groove is the Salesforce-native option. The native layer is powerful but heavy.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Salesforce Sales Engagement, the native cadence layer inside the CRM, is capable, but two things send teams looking. It is heavy: setup, admin, and ongoing configuration are real work, usually needing dedicated ops resource to run well. And it is inward-facing, built to work the contacts already in Salesforce rather than to source net-new prospects at scale. Add the evolving consumption pricing around Agentforce SDR, $2 per conversation, or Flex Credits at $0.10 per standard action, and buyers start asking what they are actually getting for the complexity. If you want the software to source and run outbound rather than orchestrate reps over existing records, that is a different category.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Comparison table","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Rank","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Tool","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Best for","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Standout capability","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Public pricing","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"}],"nodeType":"table-row"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"1","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Artisan","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"The AI sourcing and running outbound","nodeType"